\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Proportion of missing values in the raw dataset.}}{19}{figure.caption.12}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Representative per-column marginal distributions, real versus all five synthetic generators. HealthGAN and the three Pythia variants track the real reference. PATE-GAN places disproportionate mass on rare/low-frequency codes and distorts both the categorical and the continuous marginals.}}{50}{figure.caption.64}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Correlation-difference heatmaps (real minus synthetic) for the worst and best generators on the joint-dependency axis: (a) PATE-GAN, the worst (PCD $0.1142$), and (b) Pythia-1B, the best (PCD $0.0206$). Saturated cells denote large residual correlation; pale cells denote faithful reproduction.}}{53}{figure.caption.69}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Two-dimensional PCA projection onto principal components estimated from the combined real-plus-synthetic table. Four generators overlap the real cloud; PATE-GAN is displaced into a disjoint region along the first principal component.}}{54}{figure.caption.71}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Gradient-Boosting ROC curves under TSTR for all five generators and the real (TRTR) reference. Legend values are the corresponding AUC-ROC scores.}}{56}{figure.caption.76}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.6}{\ignorespaces Feature-importance agreement with the real-trained random-forest reference. Scores are based on the $L_1$ distance between normalised importance vectors; higher values indicate closer agreement.}}{57}{figure.caption.78}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces Consolidated privacy diagnostics across the five generators: (a)~synthetic-to-real nearest-neighbour distance on a log scale, (b)~membership-inference AUC against the random-guess baseline, (c)~attribute-inference advantage per attribute, and (d)~outlier versus non-outlier linkability.}}{62}{figure.caption.87}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.8}{\ignorespaces Privacy-utility landscape across the five generators. The horizontal axis reports predictive utility (Gradient-Boosting TSTR AUC-ROC), and the vertical axis reports median NNDR, where values above $1.0$ indicate that the median synthetic-to-real distance is not below the real-to-real reference scale. For readability, the PATE-GAN marker is shown at a capped y-position; its true median NNDR is $104.6$, as indicated by the annotation. This inflated value reflects off-manifold output rather than usable privacy protection. PATE-GAN is included for landscape completeness and interpreted as the GAN family's DP-enforced operating point (\S \ref {sec:discussion:limit:pategan-dual-role}).}}{64}{figure.caption.89}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.9}{\ignorespaces Utility Radar Comparison across six min-max scaled utility axes: AUC-ROC, F1, $1-$KS, $1-$CorrDiff, Cox confidence-interval overlap, and feature-importance agreement. Larger radius indicates stronger relative utility on the plotted axis.}}{65}{figure.caption.90}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.10}{\ignorespaces Utility-privacy heatmap across the five generators. Utility metrics are oriented as performance and privacy metrics as risk, each min-max scaled to $[0,1]$ across the generators. Only the leakage side of the middle-ideal privacy metrics is counted, so a distributionally collapsed generator can appear low-risk in the privacy block and must be read together with the summary table of Table~\ref {tab:rq2:summary}.}}{66}{figure.caption.91}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.11}{\ignorespaces Within-family differential-privacy transitions on the privacy-utility plane. Each arrow runs from the non-private to the differentially private variant of one family: HealthGAN $\to $ PATE-GAN (GAN family) and Pythia-1B $\to $ Pythia-1B-DP (LLM family). The vertical axis is logarithmic; PATE-GAN's high NNDR is the off-manifold artefact of Section~\ref {sec:results:rq2:privacy:nn}.}}{71}{figure.caption.95}%
